{#
  A list of links to the wiki pages under a path, embedded in page bodies
  through the Templetor macro beside this file.

  Everything that reads the request stays in that wrapper: the ?path= and
  ?page= values, and homepath(), which is web.ctx.homepath. Called from
  FastAPI, a request read inside a template can return a value left over from
  another visitor's request -- see "only the route touches the request" in
  docs/core/fastapi-pages.md.

  The page lookup stays there too, so this template only renders what it is
  handed and a FastAPI route can fetch the pages its own way.

  `pages` is a sequence of Things, each with .key and .type.key.
#}
{% macro page_list(pages, homepath="") %}
    <!--islist-->
    <ul>
        {% for p in pages %}
            {% if p.type.key != '/type/delete' %}
                <li>
                    <a href="{{ homepath }}{{ p.key }}">{{ p.key }}</a>
                </li>
            {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
{% endmacro %}
{#- Rendering this file directly (from the Templetor wrapper) draws the list.
    Guarded so that importing the macro does not render the body, which would
    raise on the undefined `pages` under StrictUndefined. -#}
{%- if pages is defined %}
    {{ page_list(pages, homepath | default("")) }}
{%- endif %}
